Summary: Add a winemetal.dll stub so DXMT's DLLs can load
Category: graphics
Kind: feature
Origin: other
  Name: dblark/macos-wine-build
  Version: 71877c1
  URL: https://github.com/dblark/macos-wine-build/blob/71877c1/patches/0004-add-winemetal-stub.patch
  Changes: configure regenerated with autoconf 2.72 (tools/make_makefiles),
    as WineHQ's own new-DLL commits do
  Note: CX 26 has no winemetal stub (CrossOver doesn't ship DXMT). Sikarugir
    10.0_8 ships it: lib/wine/{x86_64,i386}-windows/winemetal.dll, whose only
    export is WineMetalEntry (a stub)
Upstream: no
Why: DXMT's d3d11.dll and dxgi.dll import winemetal.dll, which DXMT ships
 (PE and Unix parts) on its DLL path (WINEDLLPATH_DXMT). Outside prefix
 setup, Wine loads a builtin DLL only if a file of that name is in the
 prefix (find_builtin_without_file in dlls/ntdll/loader.c), so without one
 DXMT's winemetal.dll and d3d11.dll fail with error 126 (shown on 10.0
 build0). Building a stub winemetal.dll makes wineboot put one in system32
 and syswow64; with DXMT's on the DLL path, loading the name loads DXMT's.
 Without DXMT, the stub loads and exports only WineMetalEntry.
Programs: none known
Enable: by WINEDLLPATH_DXMT (ntdll-renderer-dll-paths) naming DXMT's DLLs; the stub file is in every prefix
Related: wine-inf-d3dmetal-placeholder-dlls; the same loader rule, met with
 wine.inf placeholders

